# Always commit and push

When the work in this conversation is done (a feature, fix, or requested change):

1. Create a git commit for the relevant files. Do not wait for the user to ask.
2. Push the branch to the remote (`git push` or `git push -u origin HEAD` if it has no upstream). Do not wait for the user to ask.

Do not commit secrets, vault PDFs, or `storage/framework/testing/disks/**`.
Do not amend unless the user asked, or a hook rewrote the commit you just made and it has not been pushed.
Do not force-push to main/master.
